-- Nested exp: the clamp is per SPINE STEP, on each step's own input. The
-- outer step maps the bound 0.5 to log 0.5 < 0, a value the inner exp can
-- never produce, so the inner step clamps it to 0 (-> -inf) instead of
-- computing log(log 0.5) = NaN. exp (exp x) > 0.5 always holds; exp (exp x)
-- < 2 iff x < log (log 2).
main = let x = Normal in if exp (exp x) > 0.5 then (if exp (exp x) < 2.0 then 1.0 else 2.0) else 3.0
